From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xorbidden <xorbidden@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:27:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MiniIOMobileFramebuffer: a panel a device's driver drives can
 take two framebuffers, and frames never tear

A device whose own driver sends the panel its frames (the Mi 9T: DSI command mode, devices/davinci) registers
a `struct hakios_panel` (hakios_panel_register): start (called by GenericARMPE before the framebuffer starts),
a second framebuffer if it can have one, the boot framebuffer's address, and show. Every frame is then drawn
into the framebuffer not shown and shown when it is whole (fb_flip=0: one, as before). Without a registered
panel nothing changes: redwood's UEFI framebuffer is drawn into as it was.

Two more causes of tearing gone, for every device: a swap's surfaces count as in use (IOSurfaceIsInUse,
MiniIOSurfaceDisplayUse) until they have been copied, and SwapEnd / SwapWait come back only then, not when
the copy starts; CoreAnimation drew into one surface in five while it was still being copied (69 of 600
layers, measured on the Mi 9T, 2026-10-23).

Seen on the Mi 9T (hackios-xnu-kernel-davinci 562d911, 1337d5f): no tearing, SpringBoard at 60 Hz.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
